__section

section__
  @title "164 — Inland Again"

  "You return inland with the scent of salt in your hair and a new humility. The land receives you like one returns home."
  courage = courage + 1

  choice__
    @target 166
    "Resume travels across the homeland"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "165 — A March Renewed"

  "You march once more, driven by a purpose that is at once clear and heavy."
  pathTaken.push("march_renewed")

  choice__
    @target 167
    "Go to the place from the ring's map"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "166 — Vault and Vigil"

  "In the vault you learn to read the small scripts carved on the bars. Time here is measured in lamps lit and doors bolted."
  lore = lore + 2

  choice__
    @target 167
    "Step out to see the world"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "167 — The Marked Vale"

  "The map brings you back to a vale where a single stone bears a new scratch — fresh, like a warning left by a traveling hand."
  lore = lore + 1

  choice__
    @target 168
    "Investigate the scratch"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "168 — The Scratch Message"

  "The scratch reads: 'Do not trust the crown.' Nearby, footprints lead toward a hill crowned with smoke."
  lore = lore + 1

  choice__
    @target 169
    "Follow the footprints"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "169 — The Hill of Smoke"

  "At the hill's top a small encampment waits, and a hooded figure offers tea and a question: 'What would you sacrifice to end it?'"
  courage = courage - 1

  choice__
    @target 170
    "Offer yourself as sacrifice"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target 171
    "Offer a plan instead"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "170 — Self-Offered"

  "Your words move the hooded figure. 'Many great things are owed to small sacrifices,' they say. They step into the ranks of your company."
  companions.push("Hooded Figure")
  courage = courage + 2

  choice__
    @target 172
    "Return to the ring's hollow"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "171 — A Plan Formed"

  "You present a plan to mislead those who seek the ring and to hide it where memory cannot follow."
  lore = lore + 2

  choice__
    @target 172
    "Put the plan into action"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "172 — The Hollow Again"

  "You return to the hollow where you once hid the ring. Moss is grown and your token sits like a small sleeping thing."
  choice__
    @target 173
    "Retrieve the ring and inspect it anew"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "173 — The Ring's Face"

  "The ring is colder now. Its dark gem is like an eye that watches your hand."
  if__ (carryingRing == false) {
    carryingRing = true
    ringName = "Hollow's Eye"
  }

  choice__
    @target 174
    "Decide to keep it safe in a new hiding place"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "174 — A Deeper Hollow"

  "You dig where roots tangle and slip the ring into a stone's cavity, sealing with a small charm and a vow of silence."
  carryingRing = false
  ringName = ""
  pathTaken.push("sealed_in_deeper_hollow")

  choice__
    @target 175
    "Move away and change your name if needed"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "175 — The Name Changed"

  "You take a new name in a new town to fool those who track by memory. It helps for a little while."
  playerName = "Wanderer"
  lore = lore + 1

  choice__
    @target 176
    "Continue under the new name"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "176 — Quiet Days"

  "Quiet days pass; gardens grow at the edges of roads and children learn new songs. You teach them how to patch boots."
  courage = courage + 1
  health = health + 5

  choice__
    @target 177
    "Stay longer"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "177 — A Risen Shadow"

  "Under a crescent moon a shadow moves through the town and the child you taught awakens, weeping."
  "Someone took the charm and the hollow is bare."
  pathTaken.push("charm_stolen")
  lore = lore + 1

  choice__
    @target 178
    "Pursue the thief"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "178 — The Chase"

  "You chase across rooftops and down alleys until you corner a small thief who holds the charm trembling."
  choice__
    @target 179
    "Question the thief gently"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target 180
    "Take the charm and the thief's purse"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "179 — Gentle Questions"

  "The thief is a scared child who took the charm for its shine. They point to a cloaked caravan on the road."
  companions.push("Thief-Child")
  lore = lore + 1

  choice__
    @target 181
    "Track the caravan"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "180 — Heavy-Handed"

  "You take the charm and some coins. The child cries but runs. You feel the weight of having chosen force."
  gold = gold + 2
  courage = courage - 1

  choice__
    @target 181
    "Follow the caravan quietly"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "181 — The Cloaked Caravan"

  "The caravan is large and guarded. At its center a crowned man sits who studies a small ring in a glass case."
  lore = lore + 2

  choice__
    @target 182
    "Sneak to the center tent"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target 183
    "Challenge the man openly"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "182 — In the Tent"

  "Inside the tent the crown's man smiles coldly. He knows more than he lets on and speaks of a 'sundered oath' that the ring breaks."
  courage = courage - 1

  choice__
    @target 184
    "Try to steal the ring back"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target 185
    "Speak to learn his aim"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "183 — Open Challenge"

  "You step into the light. The caravan guards laugh at first, then circle. Your friends stand with you; the air tastes of iron."
  health = health - 10

  choice__
    @target 184
    "Fight to reclaim the ring"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "184 — A Swift Theft"

  "In the bustle you slip a hand into the case and steal the ring. It slips onto your finger and the tent closes like a trap."
  carryingRing = true
  courage = courage - 2

  choice__
    @target 186
    "Sprint from the tent"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "185 — Learning the Aim"

  "He says: 'I will make it a tool to bind kings to order. With this, I will end war or crown myself.'"
  courage = courage - 1

  choice__
    @target 186
    "Try to dissuade him"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "186 — Fleeing the Caravan"

  "You run through wagons and mud. Arrows stick, but your feet are fleet. At last you slip into a copse and breathe."
  health = health - 5

  choice__
    @target 187
    "Decide what to do with the ring now"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "187 — The Weight Again"

  "By moonlight the ring glows faintly. You feel power and danger coiled together like twin serpents."
  choice__
    @target 188
    "Seize power to force peace"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target 189
    "Destroy it if you can"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target 190
    "Hide it until better days"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "188 — Power's Promise"

  "You imagine stopping wars, making laws that heal, holding a hand that steadies thousands."
  courage = courage + 1

  choice__
    @target 191
    "Use the ring to take action"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "189 — Forge and Fire"

  "You return to the Deepforge where flames once licked at the ring. The smiths watch and they measure ash."
  choice__
    @target 192
    "Try to melt it again"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "190 — Hiding"

  "You hide the ring in a place where only you and the oldest friends know. You travel slowly, living small days."
  pathTaken.push("hid_secretly_again")
  lore = lore + 1

  choice__
    @target 193
    "Live the quiet life while watching for danger"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "191 — Seizing Action"

  "With the ring's whisper at your shoulder you command a small wane: wars end, but calm is brittle and built on fear."
  courage = courage - 2
  lore = lore + 1

  choice__
    @target 194
    "Continue wielding power"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "192 — Melting Trial"

  "The ring resists the heat as a living thing, and the smiths' faces go pale. Fire cannot hold what is bound to will."
  if__ (courage >= 15) {
    "With will and ancient words you temper flame until the ring softens like wax, then cracks and dissolves."
    carryingRing = false
    ringName = ""
    lore = lore + 5
  } else__ {
    "The flame spits and the ring remains whole; something in the forges croaks like a bird."
    health = health - 10
  }

  choice__
    @target 195
    "Leave the forge"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "193 — Quiet Watching"

  "Years pass with small joys — harvests, children's laughter, the comfort of dawn. But you always glance behind trees."
  courage = courage - 1
  lore = lore + 1

  choice__
    @target 195
    "Decide whether the safety is enough"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "194 — The Price of Order"

  "Order built by command breeds a slow bitterness. Murmurs grow; some call your rule tyranny in new clothes."
  courage = courage - 2

  choice__
    @target 196
    "Renounce the ring"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target 197
    "Hold fast and tighten control"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "195 — After the Trial"

  "You walk away from the forge with dust and heated iron on your boots. The world still moves; choices remain open."
  choice__
    @target 198
    "Go to the valley and see what others do"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "196 — Renunciation"

  "You place the ring upon a stone and speak a vow of renunciation. Tears fall and the ring warms, then cools."
  carryingRing = false
  ringName = ""
  pathTaken.push("renounced_ring")
  lore = lore + 3

  choice__
    @target 198
    "Leave it where it rests and step back"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "197 — Tightening Control"

  "You clamp down, laws are enforced, enemies made. For a time peace reigns, but under it, rot."
  health = health - 20
  courage = courage - 2

  choice__
    @target 199
    "Face the consequences"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "198 — Valley's Choice"

  "People argue at the valley. Some say the ring must be destroyed; others say it must be used wisely."
  choice__
    @target 200
    "Encourage destruction"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target 201
    "Argue for custodial secrecy"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "199 — Consequence Day"

  "Revolt comes in whispers and then in swords. You learn that power taken without consent is brittle and sharp."
  health = health - 30
  courage = courage - 3

  choice__
    @target 202
    "Surrender the ring and seek atonement"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "200 — Destruction Attempt"

  "At a common council you propose to break the ring by joint effort. Many hands together bend the will of small things."
  if__ (lore >= 35) {
    "With song, iron, and oath, the ring cracks and falls silent. The world exhales and a great weight lifts."
    carryingRing = false
    ringName = ""
    lore = lore + 5
  } else__ {
    "Without knowledge and song the attempt fails; the ring laughs and slips away to hiding."
    carryingRing = true
    lore = lore - 2
  }

  choice__
    @target 203
    "Mark the new path forward"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "201 — Custody Secured"

  "You argue for guarded custody. The vault is deemed the safer bet. The ring is sealed away under watch."
  pathTaken.push("vaulted_ring")
  carryingRing = false
  ringName = ""
  lore = lore + 2

  choice__
    @target 203
    "Become one of the wardens"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "202 — Surrender and Atonement"

  "You lay down arms and names in a small ceremony. Forgiveness is hard but honest; people heal slowly."
  courage = courage + 2
  health = health + 10

  choice__
    @target 203
    "Live quietly and help rebuild"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "203 — Epilogue Beginnings"

  "Whichever path you chose, the land moves on. Fields recover. Children laugh. Songs change and adapt like rivers."
  "You keep memories, and you keep a responsibility to speak when small things become too heavy."

  choice__
    @target 204
    "Hear the closing words"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "204 — Closing Words"

  "Tales do not end; they fold into new beginnings. The ring, where it rests, is a lesson in how simple things can hold dangers and grace alike."
  "You, ${playerName}, have seen much and learned that the largest choices are often made in the smallest acts."

  choice__
    @target 205
    "Read a final recounting of the journey"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "205 — Recounting"

  "You recall the roads: Bridge, Tower, Bell, Forge, Sea. Each step was an answer to a question you were afraid to ask."
  "The company you formed was imperfect but true. You learned of courage, of the cost and of the quiet joys."

  choice__
    @target 206
    "Receive the last blessing"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "206 — The Last Blessing"

  "An elder lays a hand on your head and speaks: 'May your name be small where it must be, and large where it helps another.'"
  courage = courage + 2

  choice__
    @target 207
    "Walk home"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "207 — Homeward"

  "The road home is not empty — it is full of people who remember you as one who chose when choices mattered."
  health = health + 10

  choice__
    @target 208
    "Return to the Hollow gate"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "208 — The Hollow Gate Revisited"

  "At the gate your oldest friend waits, older but smiling. The world has been wide and you have been part of its change."
  choice__
    @target 209
    "Sit and share a silent cup"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "209 — The Silent Cup"

  "You drink and listen to the small daily sounds — a distant child, a dog barking, a saucepan clank. Peace is made of such fragments."
  choice__
    @target 210
    "Lay down your pack and tie a token on the gate"
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "210 — A Token on the Gate"

  "You tie a simple token — a scrap of cloth or a hammered coin — to the gate. It flaps in the breeze like a small vow."
  "This story is one of many; new voices will pick up the road where you left off."

  "THE END (for this telling — other paths remain.)"
__section
